# What never needs to leave this machine.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory, not the git tree, so anything
# gitignored still ships unless it is named here. That is how 234 MB of local
# supplier cache ended up traced into every serverless function and pushed
# fourteen of them past the size limit — a failure that says "function too
# large" and gives no hint that the cause is a directory the deployment never
# reads.
#
# `.data` is the local catalogue cache. On serverless the runtime writes to
# /tmp/nazil/data instead (lib/server/runtime.ts), so this directory is dead
# weight in a deployment. `data-seed` is the committed seed and is deliberately
# traced in by next.config.ts — it must not be listed here.
#
# One caveat, learned the hard way: this is incompatible with
# `vercel deploy --prebuilt`. A local `next build` prerenders pages, which
# touches the store and leaves `.data/agencies.json` referenced in the build
# output; shipping that output without the directory fails with a bare
# `ENOENT ... /vercel/path0/.data/agencies.json` that names no cause. Deploy
# with a remote build — there is no `.data` on the builder, so nothing looks
# for it.
.data

# Local harness output and scratch.
.next/cache
*.log
